# Milestone: v0.14.0-refoundation
# Covers: a `&` join where one arm PARKS, run as a deployed script rather
#         than a REPL line.  `urbi_run` pumps only until nothing is READY,
#         which is the right cadence for a REPL but truncates a batch
#         program: before the CLI grew its own pump loop, everything after
#         the 5ms sleep was silently dropped and the process still exited
#         0.  The `1` on the last line is the whole point -- it can only
#         be read after the sleeping arm has woken and the join completed.
#
#         Line mode cannot host this: under -i each statement is its own
#         chunk, so the fork and the read never share a pump.
# matrix-row: separator-and

## mode: file

var done = 0;
{ sleep(5ms); done = 1 } & { echo("arm") };
echo(done)
[00000000] *** arm
[00000000] *** 1
